{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027040-storytelling-system-as-a-generic-rpg","id":1027040,"title":"Storytelling System as a Generic RPG?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-05T08:20:20-08:00","id":1027040,"title":"Storytelling System as a Generic RPG?","content":"I would love to see the Storytelling system as a generic system. For several years I have been running and playing Savage Worlds and enjoyed the fact that I could use the same system for multiple genres. But there are issues with Savage Worlds as there are with any system and it doesn't work as well for every playing style or every genre. I recently decided to use Storytelling system for a straightforward Space Opera game using elements from Second Sight for Psionics and Mirrors: Infinite Macabre for Alien races. Turned out this was not so hard to do but it did take some work. It reminded me how great the Storytellig system really is and how easy it would be to adapt to lots of other styles of play and genres. I would love to encourage Onyx Path to produce a pdf geared at bringing together all the potential options for using the system in multiple rpg genres. Maybe they could even take a leaf out of the Savage world or Fate book and have a licence to use this generic version of the system for people who want to use it for their settings. It doesn't seem like it would take a great amount of work to do this by Onx path and i don't see a downside. The upside is that we who love this system could use it for more than just the NWod/CofD games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:31:52-08:00","id":1027049,"title":"","content":"There are two downsides that I can see:<br /> <br /> 1. It takes work to create and maintain a system, adding a generic* system to the mix would be a lot of work for what might be little reward.<br /> <br /> 2. The Storytelling system is owned by White Wolf Publishing not Onyx Path. OnyxPath has the license to create CofD using it, but have to get apporvals from White Wolf. It would have to be White Wolf that decides to use the system in that fashion. Onyx Path does own the StoryPath system (see Scion and Trinity) and they could add additional games using it if they wanted.<br /> <br /> *Generic isn't really the correct way to look at it. The CofD core book really is about as generic as you can get (plus some horror stuff). Other 'generic' systems just have lots of different setting materials available for the different settings (usually less fleshed out and rich than you get from a more focused game line).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:33:57-08:00","id":1027050,"title":"","content":"Generic-ness isn't only about setting and flavor. CofD's iteration of Storytelling system is tilted towards psychodrama and horror narrative play on fundamental, game-mechanics level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:39:18-08:00","id":1027054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027040-storytelling-system-as-a-generic-rpg?p=1027050#post1027050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generic-ness isn't only about setting and flavor. CofD's iteration of Storytelling system is tilted towards psychodrama and horror narrative play on fundamental, game-mechanics level.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not sure if this was for me or scifirabbi, but I agree. It's why I said 'about as generic'; it does bring some other things to the table indeed. Also ties into my parenthetical in my footnote: Generic means that the core system lacks that and if you want to do horror then you have to add a system on for it and it would be less elegant and fully fleshed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T09:19:01-08:00","id":1027073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027040-storytelling-system-as-a-generic-rpg?p=1027054#post1027054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not sure if this was for me or scifirabbi, but I agree. It's why I said 'about as generic'; it does bring some other things to the table indeed. Also ties into my parenthetical in my footnote: Generic means that the core system lacks that and if you want to do horror then you have to add a system on for it and it would be less elegant and fully fleshed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the feedback. Good to know about who owns the system. That does make things more complicated but still not impossible. <br /> <br /> As for the genericness of the system, it is true that the system is geared more towards narrative and psychological. But that's good. There is no such thing as a truly generic system, they all have certain flavors and priorities. That's one of the reasons I started looking for an alternative to Savage Worlds in the first place. that system is great but better for high action and explosive pulp action (lots of random explody dice in the system). <br /> <br /> But the Storytelling system has lots of options for more or less horror, more or less action, more or less gritty combat etc. The system as it exists is one that has lots of toolkit options and these could be used for adapting to different play styles and genres. It couldn't fit for everything but as i said, no generic system really can anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T09:43:39-08:00","id":1027084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027040-storytelling-system-as-a-generic-rpg?p=1027073#post1027073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback. Good to know about who owns the system. That does make things more complicated but still not impossible.<br /> <br /> As for the genericness of the system, it is true that the system is geared more towards narrative and psychological. But that's good. There is no such thing as a truly generic system, they all have certain flavors and priorities. That's one of the reasons I started looking for an alternative to Savage Worlds in the first place. that system is great but better for high action and explosive pulp action (lots of random explody dice in the system).<br /> <br /> But the Storytelling system has lots of options for more or less horror, more or less action, more or less gritty combat etc. The system as it exists is one that has lots of toolkit options and these could be used for adapting to different play styles and genres. It couldn't fit for everything but as i said, no generic system really can anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess the question then is, what is it you actually want? You said you used Mirrors for the SciFi stuff. There are other (1e at least) Mirrors hacks available for other settings, as well as Dark Eras and other historical setting books. And changing the grittyness and action level, etc. So aside form branding it as generic what do you think would be a good change?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T09:55:38-08:00","id":1027091,"title":"","content":"IMHO, StoryTelling system enough generic for any kind social game in any setting. Less tactic and more dramatic combat. Less master arbitrariness more player suggestion. This rules force socialization. For tactic combat i should recommend another rules. Narration for social encounter, for combat encounter, for supernatural encounter. You should use this system when Story dominate above other elements.<br /> For me i used it for postapocalyptic nanopank SciFi (core + mage for technicians + vampire for mutants).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:01:46-08:00","id":1027100,"title":"","content":"What i would like is a document that provided all the tools that already exist and create a few new ones to provide a one stop toolkit for using the basic system for different genres and not just for WoD in space or transposing the existing splats into different eras or settings. this could include various options for more or less gritty, more or less action etc, conditions for different genres (space, fantasy etc). New skills and new specializations, new merits for different genres and new equipment. Also adapting rules for alien race creation in infinite macabre for other races in other genres. And more clarity on what defines a major template vs a minor template and how to crate them for yourself. <br /> <br /> Like i said, most of this does already exist in one form or another in various different places and books. all I want is the extra work to adapt it all to provide a unified document that provides all of it in one place and gives guidance on how to use the rules for multiple genres and play styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:08:27-08:00","id":1027107,"title":"","content":"I doubt that's ever going to happen. It's a lot of work for something that's not very sought for. Besides, 90% of that document would still just be taken from the core book so anyone who wants to use the system in other game styles is better of just adapting the core book than paying for something they probably already own (or otherwise they wouldn't want to use this system to begin with).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:17:59-08:00","id":1027118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027040-storytelling-system-as-a-generic-rpg?p=1027107#post1027107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt that's ever going to happen. It's a lot of work for something that's not very sought for. Besides, 90% of that document would still just be taken from the core book so anyone who wants to use the system in other game styles is better of just adapting the core book than paying for something they probably already own (or otherwise they wouldn't want to use this system to begin with).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well it could be done by referring to the main book and just having a document that includes all the widgets i.e. all the added toolkits for adapting to other settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:27:35-08:00","id":1027131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027040-storytelling-system-as-a-generic-rpg?p=1027107#post1027107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt that's ever going to happen. It's a lot of work for something that's not very sought for. Besides, 90% of that document would still just be taken from the core book so anyone who wants to use the system in other game styles is better of just adapting the core book than paying for something they probably already own (or otherwise they wouldn't want to use this system to begin with).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As for it not being sought for, you are correct that i may the only one who is currently clamoring for this! But i think this was a missed opportunity when other systems were doing the same. Basic Roleplaying came from Call of Cthulhu, FATE I believe came from Spirit of the Century, etc. This is an area of the rpg market that is being taken advantage of by other companies with other systems. I think the Storytelling system is one of the best systems around and would love to be able to use it more easily in many different genres. And maybe others would too if it were effectively marketed that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:38:29-08:00","id":1027137,"title":"","content":"While I will chime in with the folks who say getting an &quot;Official&quot; Genre-Neutral kit for CofD is unlikely, I can provide some advice on what are your best resources.<br /> <br /> As my key resources, I use <i><b>Armory 2</b></i>, and <i><b>Mirrors</b></i>. While both are 1rst edition books, Armory gives a entire section on how to alter the combat mechanics to suit a particular play style (from heroic high action, to gritty and deadly). Mirrors also offers many examples of how to adjust the baseline setting to accommodate different genres.<br /> <br /> I also use <i><b>Hunter:the Vigil</b></i> extensively. The &quot;Endowment&quot; framework of Merits (and the tools for creating your own) are some of my favorite toolkit mechanics in the system. More recently, <i><b>Hurt Locker</b></i> also provides several very interesting mechanical options, and provides a good look at creating &quot;Minor&quot; templates.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Dark Eras</b></i> give good examples of historical genres and has good advice for adjusting the skill selection to fit different time periods (which can be used for different genres as well).<br /> <br /> Stepping briefly outside the WoD/CofD , <i><b>GURPS</b></i> has probably some of the best researched sourcebooks for playing in different eras and genres. While I am not a big fan of the system itself, its resources are quite excellent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:45:35-08:00","id":1027143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027040-storytelling-system-as-a-generic-rpg?p=1027137#post1027137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I will chime in with the folks who say getting an &quot;Official&quot; Genre-Neutral kit for CofD is unlikely, I can provide some advice on what are your best resources.<br /> <br /> As my key resources, I use <i><b>Armory 2</b></i>, and <i><b>Mirrors</b></i>. While both are 1rst edition books, Armory gives a entire section on how to alter the combat mechanics to suit a particular play style (from heroic high action, to gritty and deadly). Mirrors also offers many examples of how to adjust the baseline setting to accommodate different genres.<br /> <br /> I also use <i><b>Hunter:the Vigil</b></i> extensively. The &quot;Endowment&quot; framework of Merits (and the tools for creating your own) are some of my favorite toolkit mechanics in the system. More recently, <i><b>Hurt Locker</b></i> also provides several very interesting mechanical options, and provides a good look at creating &quot;Minor&quot; templates.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Dark Eras</b></i> give good examples of historical genres and has good advice for adjusting the skill selection to fit different time periods (which can be used for different genres as well).<br /> <br /> Stepping briefly outside the WoD/CofD , <i><b>GURPS</b></i> has probably some of the best researched sourcebooks for playing in different eras and genres. While I am not a big fan of the system itself, its resources are quite excellent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good to know. And you are correct that GURPS has some great supplements but a less than stellar system. <br /> <br /> Is there anywhere that clarifies rules for major and minor templates?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T11:00:13-08:00","id":1027155,"title":"","content":"So assuming my hope for a single document is a pipe dream, lets see if we can collect resources and suggestions for various options:<br /> <br /> Armory 2 for combat options<br /> Mirrors for genres changes (but having looked at Mirrors there is less crunch there than i would like)<br /> Hunter: The Vigil endowments<br /> Mirrors: Infinite Macabre for spaceships and race creation mechanics<br /> Hurt Locker for minor templates <br /> Dark eras for historical settings<br /> <br /> <br /> What else is out there? Can you expand one what Hurt locker has about minor templates and how the endowments in Hunter work?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T12:11:10-08:00","id":1027204,"title":"","content":"Also, what about different approaches to magi. Obviously there is Mage and also the lower magic in second sight. Anything else? How does the &quot;magic&quot; system in the Hunter Witch book work. is it just a streamlined version of mage or is it different enough to be its own thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T12:36:43-08:00","id":1027222,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Minor Templates and Endowments</b><br /> <br /> The concept of Minor Templates have been in the system from pretty much the beginning, but the application has varied greatly across the board. I recommend Hurt Lockers approach because its very easy to work with ( essentially the character has access to a &quot;base Merit&quot; that serves as the foundation of its special powers and typically one or two extra mechanics to flesh out the Template).<br /> <br /> As for Endowments, they are essentially a set of merits that require belonging to one of the Hunter organizations as a prerequisite. They range from merits that give access to special equipment to flat-out supernatural powers (and cover a lot of ground in between). Probably the most useful element in the Hunter book is a section that gives guidelines for developing new endowments.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Mortal Magic</b><br /> <br /> The Gutter Magic system from <i><b>Witchhunter</b></i> more than anything was to provide a robust magic system for those that didn't want to try and incorate the magic system for Mage but still wanted good Spellcasting foils for a Hunter Cell. It is quite different than the Mage system - overall much simpler and more general.They are set up very much in the style of a minor template, and likely served as a inspiration for how minor templates were approached in later books.<br /> <br /> However, the sourcebook <i><b>Second Sight</b></i> also gives a way to present mortal-level occult powers. Its an early first edition book and shows its age design-wise, but it gives some good insight into how to go about designing similar content.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T12:45:38-08:00","id":1027226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027040-storytelling-system-as-a-generic-rpg?p=1027204#post1027204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, what about different approaches to magi. Obviously there is Mage and also the lower magic in second sight. Anything else? How does the &quot;magic&quot; system in the Hunter Witch book work. is it just a streamlined version of mage or is it different enough to be its own thing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Different enough to be its own thing, but there are similarities.<br /> <br /> Any Gameline's &quot;Special Powers&quot; can be rehashed as magic systems to varying degrees of flexibility and metaphysical implication (I can provide examples, if desired). Out of Core, you can also just slap Influences and Numina on a character and call them a Mage, if you want (I started a thread on this a while back).<br /> <br /> The Horrors sub-system in Chronicles of Darkness Core (as opposed to the GMC rules update) can cover pretty much every other creature you can think off. Check out <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a>'s threads in their signature for some great examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":".  Cleaned up. 01-05-2017, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T21:43:08-08:00","id":1027438,"title":"","content":"I would honestly wait and use Storypath instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T16:27:16-08:00","id":1027908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\">